metalive <publicREMOVE@THISmetalive.net> wrote:
>Douglas Henke wrote:
>> Take potions for example. You get clear=water for free. Dipping a
>> dart in unknown potions will reveal poison and polymorph, two of the
>> really bad ones. A unihorn will convert most of the other unpleasant
>> ones to water (or cure their effects if you drink them). That leaves
>> acid (a minor nuisance once you grow a few HP) and sleep (test inside
>> a small, safe locked room). I usually stockpile potions until I get
>> a unihorn, dip darts to find poison/poly, try the rest in a safe area,
>> and convert "bad" potions to holy water. (Never test cursed potions,
>> or anything else cursed.)
>
>-What is a unihorn?

Unicorn horn, obtained by killing a unicorn.

>-If I've understood you correctly, the clear potion is ALWAYS plain 
>water? What is plain water good for?

Yes.  You can turn it into holy water or unholy water.

>-What is holy water good for?

Blessing things, mostly.  Unholy water curses things.  Surprisingly,
there are one or two items which do very useful things when they are
cursed.

(Holy water has a couple of other uses; you can throw it at undead to
hurt them, or [IIRC] drink it to cure food poisoning.)

>Other misc questions:
>-What are gems good for? (If I happen to find one which isn't just a 
>worthless piece of coloured glass.)

They are worth a lot of money... if you've identified them.  Also, an
identified non-glass gem can be thrown at a unicorn of your alignment
(if you can line it up) to get a large luck boost.  Lining up a shot on
a unicorn is virtually impossible unless you are at least "fast" *and*
unburdened.

>-What does "Beware, fullmoon tonight!" indicate?

Full moon.  +1 base luck; dogs are harder to tame; werefoos appear in
their foo form, not their human form.

>-What can I do with blank scrolls?

Write on them with magic markers to make more useful scrolls.  Or
polypile them, same objective.

>-I know from a spoiler, that my reward for solving sokoban, is a bag of 
>holding. However, I haven't identified it as such yet, but am already 
>using it. What is it's maximum capacity? Can it store even more, when 
>identified?

Like any container in Nethack, a bag of holding can hold an arbitrarily
large amount of stuff; this stuff has its weight reduced by 50% (uncursed
bag) or 75% (blessed bag), or increased by 100% if the bag is cursed.

Furthermore, a cursed bag destroys some of its own contents every time it
is opened.  Never carry your entire supply of holy water or scrolls of
remove curse in a bag of holding, and always check the blessed/cursed
status of your bag before opening it.
